      "lineNbr": 778,
      "author": {
        "id": 1989777
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-11T10:07:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes although it\u0027s not really our intention that users of the simulator will ever have to worry about this. While users could start using the simulator after the [stage 1 setup](https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/art/+/2680028/6), it is expected that it will be much more useful after some of the later patches which enable more compilation.\n\nThe compilation filter allows us to gradually enable the simulator by enabling instructions individually. To begin with we don\u0027t compile anything apart from these special `$compile$` methods and we test a few basic methods this way in the [stage 1 simulator setup](https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/art/+/2680028/7/test/2237-checker-simulator/src/Main.java). After this we begin enabling more instructions and this marker again allows us to test this, https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/art/+/2680029/6/test/2237-checker-simulator/src/Main.java. Lastly we [remove the compilation filter](https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/art/+/2901294/5/compiler/optimizing/optimizing_compiler.cc#b1198) altogether and rely on the existing ART tests to provide us good testing coverage.",
      "parentUuid": "b9c95555_7ddb336d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 778,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 778,
        "endChar": 93
      },
      "revId": "5deedd61a15d934edf3f76c0f8181054d8a140f9",
