    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6f11cc5a_6829a2c5",
        "filename": "compiler/optimizing/optimizing_compiler.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 995,
      "author": {
        "id": 1989777
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-11T10:07:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From a high level perspective, the simulator is only simulating the optimized code output from the codegen so we want to check whether the method can be compiled (simulated) just before this moment, as that IR will reflect what we will actually be simulating. We don\u0027t want to check whether the method can be compiled (simulated) before we run those optimizations.\n\nFor the [stage 1 setup](https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/art/+/2680028/6) this doesn\u0027t matter because the compilation filter doesn\u0027t check the graph anyway but [later patches](https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/art/+/2901291/5) will check the graph.",
      "parentUuid": "35d14261_13a0a895",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 995,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 995,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "5deedd61a15d934edf3f76c0f8181054d8a140f9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
