      "lineNbr": 1941,
      "author": {
        "id": 1989777
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-11T10:07:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The function signature of a critical native method won\u0027t have the first two arguments (the JNI environment and jclass) of a regular native method however it could have other arguments which still need to be passed through. Because of this, it\u0027s not safe to pass through these first two arguments. For example:\n\n```cpp\n// On entry:\n// x0 \u003d JNIEnv\n// x1 \u003d jclass\n// x2 \u003d a\n// x3 \u003d b\n// x4 \u003d c\nstatic jint Java_Main_intFastNativeMethod(JNIEnv*, jclass, jint a, jint b, jint c);\n\n// x0 \u003d a\n// x1 \u003d b\n// x2 \u003d c\nstatic jint Java_Main_intCriticalNativeMethod(jint a, jint b, jint c);\n```\n\nWe need to know whether those first two arguments are included or not because otherwise a, b and c won\u0027t be in the expected registers for the native code.",
      "parentUuid": "ff8458cc_2522f681",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1933,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1941,
        "endChar": 0
      },
